  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a cuboid of sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and a closed hemisphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>. If the sum of their surface areas is constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>, then the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>r</mi></math>, for which the sum of their volumes is maximum, is"
  },
